tarian Cuisine]] | [[Cookbook:Holiday Recipes|Holiday Recipes]] | [[Cookbook:Pie|Pies]] | [[Cookbook:Dessert|Dessert]]\n==Ingredients==\n\n===Filling===\n* 1 package (8 [[Cookbook:Ounce|ounces]]) [[Cookbook:Cream Cheese|cream cheese]]\n* ⅓ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] white granulated [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* ¼ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]]\n* 1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Vanilla Extract|vanilla extract]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Each|ea]]. 9-[[Cookbook:Inch|inch]] unbaked [[Cookbook:Pie Crust|pie shell]], or single homemade pie crust\n* 1¼ cups [[Cookbook:Chop|chopped]] [[Cookbook:Pecan|pecans]]\n\n===Topping===\n* 3 eggs\n* 1 cup [[Cookbook:Corn Syrup|light corn syrup]]\n* ¼ cup white granulated sugar\n* 1 teaspoon vanilla extract\n\n==Procedure==\n# Preheat [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] to [[Cookbook:Oven_temperatures|375°F]].\n# Combine the cream cheese, sugar, and salt; [[Cookbook:Beat|beat]] until smooth.\n# Add egg and vanilla, beating well after each.\n# Spoon mixture into unbaked pie shell. Sprinkle with pecans.\n# Combine 3 eggs, corn syrup, remaining sugar, and vanilla; beat well.\n# Pour this mixture over pecans.\n# [[Cookbook:Bake|Bake]] for 35–40 minutes or until set.\n\n[[Category:Inexpensive recipes]]\n[[Category:Southern U.S. recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for pecan pie]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pecan]]\n[[Category:Recipes using nuts and seeds]]\n[[Category:Baking recipes]]\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes for dessert]]\n[[Category:Recipes using granulated sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using corn syrup]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cream cheese]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Layered Pecan Pie","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 package (8 ounces) cream cheese","sourceText":"1 package (8 ounces) cream cheese","amountText":"1 package (8 ounces) cream cheese","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id"